    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.8"/>
    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Wheeze, cough and breathlessness this winter, for about three months: symptoms on three or four days a week, waking with cough and a tight chest about twice a month, breathless climbing the hill streets in cold air; worse with cold wind, kitchen and fireplace smoke, and colds; called a weak chest and asthma since childhood but never tested or treated. Asthma to be confirmed with spirometry before and after bronchodilator and FeNO: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Work-up of wheeze and cough: chest X-ray, blood count with eosinophils, interferon-gamma release assay for tuberculosis infection (born in a country where tuberculosis is common), and a urine pregnancy test before treatment; no inhaler is started before testing unless symptoms worsen. Guideline: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); Latent Tuberculosis Infection in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item>Trauma-informed, patient-centred care: seen alone for part of every visit; consent, information and results to her alone, through her own contact details; no instructions about her care accepted from the household; private screening for safety and exploitation at each visit, with resources and social work offered and her decisions respected. Guideline: Intimate Partner Violence and Caregiver Abuse of Older or Vulnerable Adults: Screening (2025); Human Trafficking: ACOG Committee Opinion, Number 787. Obstet Gynecol 2019;134(3):e90-e95 (PMID 31441827) (2019) [S]</item><item>Equity safeguards: spirometry read with race-neutral GLI Global equations, plain explanation of every result, and attention to the higher asthma burden carried by Black women. Guideline: Bhakta NR, et al. Race and Ethnicity in Pulmonary Function Test Interpretation: An Official American Thoracic Society Statement. Am J Respir Crit Care Med 2023;207(8):978-995 (PMID 36973004) (2023); Pate CA, et al. Asthma Surveillance - United States, 2006-2018. MMWR Surveill Summ 2021;70(5):1-32 (PMID 34529643) (2021) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to pulmonology, Gideon Fairbanks-Mensah, MD, ordered 1773-02-09 [S]</item></list></text>

